;;-*-Lisp-*-
(in-package goal)

;; name: paddywagon-v.gc
;; name in dgo: paddywagon-v
;; dgos: CWI

#|
  ============================================================================
  paddywagon-v.gc -- MOD jak2/features/paddywagon/traffic
  ============================================================================

  Puts the Krimzon Guard PADDY WAGON (prisoner transport) into Haven City's
  ambient ground traffic, carrying a random civilian prisoner in its rear cage
  and piloted by a Crimson Guard -- drivable and stealable exactly like every
  other guard vehicle.

  WHY A NEW TYPE INSTEAD OF REUSING `paddywagon`
  ----------------------------------------------
  The retail `paddywagon` type lives in levels/city/meet-brutter/meet-brutter.gc,
  which ships in LMEETBRT.DGO -- a *borrowed* mission level. It is not loaded in
  free roam, and it is deliberately un-stealable:
    * `init-skel-and-rigid-body` re-homes the process onto 'lmeetbrt (so its art
      resolves from the mission DGO) and sets `rigid-body-object-flag no-hijack`,
      which is what `vehicle-util.gc`'s boarding probe tests before it will even
      show the "press triangle" prompt;
    * `vehicle-method-134` / `vehicle-method-108` / the `hostile` + `active` state
      overrides implement the meet-brutter chase, not city traffic behaviour;
    * its `object-type` is #x13 -- it impersonates the hellcat.
  So this file defines a sibling, `paddywagon-v`, that is a plain traffic
  `vehicle-guard`: same hull, same physics constants, none of the mission
  scaffolding. Retail `paddywagon` is left completely untouched, so the
  meet-brutter mission is bit-for-bit unchanged.

  WHAT COMES FOR FREE FROM `vehicle-guard`
  ----------------------------------------
    | need                     | inherited from                                |
    |--------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|
    | Crimson Guard pilot      | `vehicle-guard::vehicle-method-137` spawns a  |
    |                          | `crimson-guard-rider` into seat 0.             |
    | red dot on the minimap   | `vehicle-guard::vehicle-method-128`            |
    |                          | (`minimap-class guard`, icon 14).              |
    | follows the city lanes   | `vehicle-guard-choose-branch`, installed by    |
    |                          | `vehicle-guard::alloc-and-init-rigid-body-...` |
    | hostile pursuit on alert | slot 20 already receives `trtflags-0` in       |
    |                          | `traffic-engine::restore-default-settings`, so |
    |                          | it is sent 'alert-begin / 'alert-end and never |
    |                          | parks -- retail already wired this slot as a   |
    |                          | ctywide guard-vehicle slot.                    |
    | player boards and drives | `vehicle::check-player-get-on` (we simply do   |
    |                          | NOT set `no-hijack`).                          |
    | STEALING IT IS A CRIME   | knocking the `crimson-guard-rider` off raises  |
    |                          | the city alert to 2 and drops a `crimson-guard`|
    |                          | -- see `vehicle-rider-event-handler`'s         |
    |                          | 'knocked-off case, flag bit 3. Identical to a  |
    |                          | stolen hellcat / guard-bike.                   |

  UNARMED BY DESIGN: the `paddy-wagon` skeleton has no gun joint (only
  "steering", "hatch", "main", "prejoint", "align"), so `turret info` is left at
  0. `turret-control-method-11` is guarded by `(when (nonzero? (-> this info)))`,
  so the inherited guard AI simply never fires. A prisoner van rams and pursues;
  it does not shoot.

  ASSET RESIDENCY (both circuits -- see
  docs/modding/tools/model_and_entity_level_injection_guide.md):
    * Circuit 1 (GOAL heap): "paddy-wagon-ag.go" + "tpage-2438.go" added to
      lwidea.gd / lwideb.gd / lwidec.gd. Traffic vehicles are re-homed onto the
      lwide level by `vehicle-init-by-other`'s `(lwide-entity-hack)`, so the art
      group must be resident in whichever lwide level is loaded.
    * Circuit 2 (Merc renderer): `extra_art_groups_by_dgo` in jak2_config.jsonc
      bakes "paddy-wagon-ag:LMEETBRT.DGO" into all three lwide .fr3 files.
      Requires `task extract`.
|#

;; ============================================================================
;; Skeleton
;; ============================================================================
;; Identical to retail `skel-paddywagon` (meet-brutter.gc) but under a distinct
;; name so the two never collide in `art-group-get-by-name` while the
;; meet-brutter mission has LMEETBRT borrowed in. `paddy-wagon` only ever had a
;; single LOD mesh, already declared out to 999999m, so there is no LOD-vanishing
;; problem to work around here.
(defskelgroup skel-paddywagon-v paddy-wagon paddy-wagon-lod0-jg paddy-wagon-idle-ja
              ((paddy-wagon-lod0-mg (meters 999999)))
              :bounds (static-spherem 0 0 0 6.4)
              :shadow paddy-wagon-shadow-mg
              :origin-joint-index 3
              )

;; ============================================================================
;; Flight / handling constants
;; ============================================================================
;; A verbatim copy of retail `*paddywagon-constants*` (meet-brutter.gc). Every
;; physics figure -- mass, inertial tensor, cm-offset-joint, thrusters,
;; stabilisers, camera string, seats -- is retail data and MUST be left alone:
;; moving `cm-offset-joint` without moving every control-point array by the same
;; vector is what flips a hover vehicle onto its back. The ONLY edit is
;; `object-type`, documented inline below.
;;
;; Notable retail values this mod depends on and deliberately keeps:
;;   :flags #xc          -- bit 3 set => the hull has a real collide-MESH prim,
;;                          so `vehicle::alloc-and-init-rigid-body-control` gives
;;                          the mesh `jak`/`player-list` and Jak can stand on and
;;                          board the van. Bit 6 (flight level) is NOT set, so it
;;                          rides the low ground lanes with the cars rather than
;;                          the hellcats' high air lane -- this is city traffic.
;;   :guard-type #x5     -- the hellcat guard slot: alert pacing and aim settings
;;                          come from `get-traffic-guard-type-settings` (see
;;                          `vehicle-guard::vehicle-method-82`).
;;   :seat-count 2       -- seat 0 (flags 1, angle 0) is the driver / player seat;
;;                          seat 1 (flags 4, angle #x8000 = 180 deg, y 819.2,
;;                          z -13107.2) is the REAR CAGE, facing backwards. This
;;                          is the seat retail drops the captured lurker into
;;                          during meet-brutter, and it is where this mod's
;;                          civilian prisoner stands.
;;   :rider-stance #x1   -- same as cara/carb/carc and the hellcat, so the
;;                          `crimson-guard-rider` uses its regular vehicle pose.
(define *paddywagon-v-constants*
  (new 'static 'rigid-body-vehicle-constants
    :info (new 'static 'rigid-body-info
      :mass 10.0
      :inv-mass 0.1
      :linear-damping 0.995
      :angular-damping 0.995
      :bounce-factor 0.1
      :friction-factor 0.05
      :cm-offset-joint (new 'static 'vector :y 2048.0 :z -2048.0 :w 1.0)
      :inertial-tensor-box (new 'static 'array meters 3 (meters 6) (meters 3) (meters 7))
      )
    :extra (new 'static 'rigid-body-object-extra-info
      :max-time-step 0.033333335
      :gravity (meters 40)
      :idle-distance (meters 50)
      :attack-force-scale 1.0
      )
    :name '*paddywagon-v-constants*
    :flags #xc
    ;; MOD: retail's mission paddywagon impersonates the hellcat (#x13 = 19) so the
    ;; guard system treats it as one. The traffic version owns slot 20 instead --
    ;; this is the field `traffic-object-spawn-params`/`traffic-engine` key off, and
    ;; what `crimson-guard`'s knock-off `case` in guard.gc reads. guard-type stays
    ;; #x5 (the hellcat guard slot) so alert pacing/aim settings are the hellcat's.
    :object-type #x14
    :guard-type #x5
    :max-engine-thrust (meters 50)
    :inv-max-engine-thrust 0.0000048828124
    :engine-response-rate 60.0
    :engine-intake-factor 1.5
    :brake-factor 3.5
    :turbo-boost-factor 1.0
    :max-xz-speed (meters 40)
    :ground-probe-distance (meters 4.5)
    :cos-ground-effect-angle 0.42261824
    :spring-lift-factor 0.3
    :air-drag-factor 1.0
    :steering-thruster-factor 5.0
    :steering-thruster-max-gain 4.0
    :steering-thruster-half-gain-speed (meters 15)
    :tire-friction-factor 0.5
    :tire-static-friction 0.55
    :tire-dynamic-friction 0.4
    :tire-dynamic-friction-speed (meters 2)
    :tire-inv-max-friction-speed 0.000034877234
    :airfoil-factor 1.0
    :drag-force-factor 1.0
    :speed-scrubbing-drag 10.0
    :speed-limiting-drag 0.5
    :pitch-control-factor 0.5
    :roll-control-factor 1.0
    :jump-thrust-factor 0.5
    :buoyancy-factor 1.0
    :player-weight 163840.0
    :player-shift-x (meters 0.6)
    :player-shift-z (meters 1)
    :target-speed-offset (meters -2)
    :turning-accel (meters 45)
    :toughness-factor 1.0
    :damage-factor 6.0
    :camera-string-min-height (meters 4.5)
    :camera-string-max-height (meters 4.5)
    :camera-string-min-length (meters 5)
    :camera-string-max-length (meters 12.5)
    :camera-min-fov 15109.688
    :camera-max-fov 17476.268
    :camera-head-offset 8192.0
    :camera-foot-offset 4096.0
    :camera-normal-max-angle-offset 182.04445
    :camera-air-max-angle-offset 5461.3335
    :camera-max-lookaround-speed 40960.0
    :seat-count 2
    :rider-stance #x1
    :grab-rail-array #f
    :seat-array (new 'static 'inline-array vehicle-seat-info 4
      (new 'static 'vehicle-seat-info :position (new 'static 'vector :y 9420.8 :z 2457.6 :w (the-as float #x10000)))
      (new 'static 'vehicle-seat-info
        :position (new 'static 'vector :y 819.2 :z -13107.2 :w (the-as float #x48000))
        )
      (new 'static 'vehicle-seat-info)
      (new 'static 'vehicle-seat-info)
      )
    :rider-hand-offset (new 'static 'inline-array vector 2
      (new 'static 'vector :x 2457.6 :y 409.6 :z 4710.4 :w 1.0)
      (new 'static 'vector :x -2457.6 :y 409.6 :z 4710.4 :w 1.0)
      )
    :explosion #f
    :engine-pitch-scale 0.25
    :engine-pitch-mod-amp 0.025
    :engine-sound-select 8
    :engine-sound (static-sound-name "vehicle-engine")
    :thrust-sound (static-sound-name "bike-thrust")
    :scrape-sound (static-sound-name "car-scrape-stn")
    :glance-sound (static-sound-name "car-glance-stn")
    :impact-sound (static-sound-name "car-impact-stn")
    :extra-sound (static-sound-name "car-by-1")
    :explosion-part #xa1
    :headlight-count 2
    :taillight-count 2
    :thruster-flame-width (meters 0.4)
    :thruster-flame-length (meters 2)
    :thruster-local-pos (new 'static 'inline-array vector 2
      (new 'static 'vector :x 15769.6 :y 4096.0 :z -15155.2 :w 1.0)
      (new 'static 'vector :x -15769.6 :y 4096.0 :z -15155.2 :w 1.0)
      )
    :exhaust-local-pos (new 'static 'inline-array vector 2
      (new 'static 'vector :x 15769.6 :y 4096.0 :z -15155.2 :w 1.0)
